  "contract_note": "Every mapped attribute answers four questions before an adapter may write it. kind: is it an input the source supplies (primitive), a value the engine recomputes (derived), a name/reference (identity), or read-only evidence (diagnostic)? basis_owner: which object supplies the base any unit conversion needs, written 'Class.attribute' -- the network-wide fallback is not a basis owner. orientation: which side, sign, or reference frame the source value is stated against. disposition: where the value ends up. Attributes not listed here take contract_defaults. Writing a 'derived' attribute is always a defect: PowerFactory recomputes it and discards the write, so the model silently differs from the Case that claims to describe it.",
  "contract_defaults": {
    "kind": "primitive",
    "basis_owner": null,
    "orientation": null,
    "disposition": "case_field"
  },
  "contracts": {
    "TypLne": {
      "cline": {
        "kind": "primitive",
        "basis_owner": "TypLne.frnom",
        "orientation": null,
        "disposition": "case_field",
        "reason": "capacitance per length; susceptance follows from it at the TYPE's own frnom. IEEE-14 is a 60 Hz project holding 50 Hz line types: converting at the network frequency raised every nonzero B1 by exactly 20 percent."
      },
      "bline": {
        "kind": "derived",
        "basis_owner": "TypLne.frnom",
        "orientation": null,
        "disposition": "diagnostic",
        "reason": "susceptance restated from cline at frnom; never written, always recomputed"
      },
      "cline0": {
        "kind": "primitive",
        "basis_owner": "TypLne.frnom",
        "orientation": null,
        "disposition": "case_field",
        "reason": "zero-sequence capacitance; same basis rule as cline"
      },
      "bline0": {
        "kind": "derived",
        "basis_owner": "TypLne.frnom",
        "orientation": null,
        "disposition": "diagnostic",
        "reason": "zero-sequence susceptance restated from cline0 at frnom"
      },
      "frnom": {
        "kind": "primitive",
        "basis_owner": null,
        "orientation": null,
        "disposition": "case_field",
        "reason": "the type's own rated frequency; it is the basis owner for cline/cline0 and must never be replaced by the project frequency"
      }
    },
